== links single-value n=65536 valuesFor: ordered vs btree-map
A: 107.1 ns per operation (median)
B: 228.3 ns per operation (median)
A needs 53.1% less time than B: B takes 2.13 times as long as A.
With 95% confidence the difference lies between 52.7% and 54% less time (B takes between 2.11 and 2.17 times as long as A).
Noise floor: 0.352%. Identical code measured against itself on this setup can look that different, so smaller differences mean nothing.
Neighbouring measurements are nearly independent (autocorrelation -0.11), so they were resampled one by one.

Verdict: RESOLVED. A is faster than B: the difference is real, as its interval excludes zero and it exceeds the noise floor.

Warnings:
  - the program holds 470 MB of live data, more than the caches of many machines; for data that size, where it lies in memory can shift the result by several points in ways the interval does not cover, and differently in the next process; run the comparison in several processes with the multiproc package

